I rebuilt the game from the ground up around active timed runs, a pan/pinch upgrade map and two prestige maps. I haven't committed or pushed anything.

I tested it in a mobile-sized browser and everything below worked:
- the old-save notice
- a full run
- the summary and collect step
- the map (buy, pan, pinch zoom, "Grow all")
- Rebloom, Supernova and save export/import
- all five abilities

I didn't try it on a physical phone. `node --check` passes on every JS file.

## What changed
- **Runs:** 30s base, growing to about 90s with upgrades. You tap moving targets: seeds, golden blooms, comets, multi-hit pods, time petals. Combos build a multiplier, purple spores break combos and cost time, and there are five active abilities with cooldown buttons. Feedback includes particles, number popups, crits, screen shake, vibration and combo banners.
- **Loop:** after a run you get a summary screen, then collect the Stardust and spend it. An uncollected summary survives a reload.
- **Upgrades only:** there are no generators or helpers anymore. The Garden map has 76 nodes in six branches and seven zones. Locked, available, owned and maxed states are visible, with future nodes greyed.
- **Prestige:** Rebloom (20-node Memory map) and Supernova (14-node Constellation map), each its own map under the Prestige tab.
- **Old saves:** a v1 save is detected and cleared, and a one-time notice appears. I tested this with a real v1 save in the browser.
- **Service worker:** cache bumped to `seedling-cosmos-v2`, and the new files (`costs.js`, `map.js`, `game.js`) are in the cache list.
- **README:** updated, and `SIM_RESULTS.md` is regenerated.

## Pacing sim
The sim runs the real run engine with a bot player and writes `SIM_RESULTS.md`.

| Player | Runs/day | Everything maxed |
|---|---|---|
| Standard | 12 | 28 days (4 weeks) |
| Casual | 6 | 45 days (6.5 weeks) |
| Dedicated | 30 | 24 days (3.4 weeks) |

- **First purchase:** after the first run, at under a minute in.
- **Purchase cadence:** the median is one purchase per run. The longest gap is about a day.
- **Prestige timing:** Rebloom becomes worthwhile around day 4 and the first Supernova around day 10–15. Zone 6 is reached around day 11–15.
- **Costs:** a calibrator, `tools/calibrate.js`, sets Garden costs from the bot's measured income and writes `js/costs.js`. Re-run it, then the sim, after changing upgrade effects.

## Things to know
- **Late-game grind:** the last couple of weeks are repeated Rebloom/Supernova cycles in the top zone, where the main new thing is Star Cores.
- **Tedious re-buying:** after a prestige you re-buy a lot of nodes. "Grow all" and the head-start perks make that bearable, but I'd watch how it feels in play.
- **Sim assumptions:** the timings depend on the bot's assumptions (2.8 taps/s, 88% accuracy, a prestige rule that fires roughly daily), so real players will vary.
- **First visit after the upgrade:** a user with the old service worker sees the old page once, then the new game on the next load.

I left `PROMPT2.md` and `claude2.log` untouched.
